range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect</span> tense and the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect Continuous</span> tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use/Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + has/have (not) + past participle <br> Question word + has/have + subject + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</li><li>to talk about experience <br></li><li> to emphasize the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">result</span> of an action </li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I've taken some turmeric.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect Continuous \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + have been + v-ing <br> Question word + have + subject + been v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</li><li>to talk about a single activity that lasts a long time <br> </li><li>to talk about an action that is repeated over a long period of time <br></li><li> to emphasize the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">action</span><br></li><li> when a long activity has just stopped</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My back has been aching since we went bowling.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's really helped me!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've been lying down <span class=\"strong\">for</span> days now. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>You use FOR to talk about how long an action has been happening (a week, 2 days, five hours, six years etc.)</li><li>You use SINCE to talk about when the action started (2010, Monday, she was a child)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've taken some turmeric."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My back has been aching <span class=\"strong\">since</span> we went bowling."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Second Conditional - Talking About Hypothetical Situations"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/>Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past verb + <span class=\"italic\">would</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"IF\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"simple past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I married Peter,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be happy.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it snowed next July,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be very surprised.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I were you,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be jumping up and down.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I were you, I'd be jumping up and down."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd get that checked out if I were you."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we went home, we'd need to have some movies to watch."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "swollen"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "enlarged; puffy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My thumb is quite swollen."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "swelling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an abnormal inflammation of the body"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", 